# MongoDB / Mongoose Patterns

## Layout
- Models live in `src/models/` — one model per file (e.g. `Product.ts`, `Order.ts`).
- Connection helper lives in `src/lib/db/mongoose.ts` — reuse a cached connection in serverless.
- Data access helpers live in `src/lib/` (e.g. `src/lib/products/`, `src/lib/orders/`) — never query MongoDB from React components.

## Rules
- Always `await connectDb()` before using models in Route Handlers / Server Components.
- Validate inputs with Zod at the API boundary before writing to MongoDB.
- Use lean() for read-only list queries when hydration is not needed.
- Prefer ObjectId refs + populate for relations (category, user, product).
- Never expose password hashes or secrets in API responses.
- Index `slug` (unique), payment IDs, and text fields used for search.

## Model shape
```ts
// ✅ GOOD — typed schema + export
import { Schema, model, models } from 'mongoose';
import type { Product } from '@/types/product';

const ProductSchema = new Schema<Product>({ /* ... */ }, { timestamps: true });
export const ProductModel = models.Product ?? model('Product', ProductSchema);
```
